+Both fixed local bases in the reversed23/25 copied-center construction
+Complete finite compatibility proof, 2026-10-08.
+
+Conclusion and provenance
+Fix BOTH L23=I+J and L25=I+J in PR34/37's reversed23/25 controlled family.
+The complete actual data family retains9 singleton pivots and blocks21,17,481.
+This is proved by the inherited universal zero identities plus a complete
+nonvanishing certificate for all4,073,300 actual triple pairs. There is no
+remaining generic factor and no finite-product argument substituting for
+this complete check. PR32's fixed-basis profiling, PR36's copied centers,
+PR34's reversed prescriptions and PR37/39 integration retain their original
+credits, along with all prior producers, topology and machine interfaces.
+The complete first and second fixed-basis internal profiles and the exact
+characteristic/assembly are separate certificates.
+
+1. One explicit rational common basis
+
+Put a=23,b=25,m=575,d=47 and I=(0,...,22). Keep the controlled permutation
+completions of first-d row labelsR=[I,22,I] and last-d inverse-column labels
+C=[I,0,I] from the inherited PR37 geometry. Set
+ K=T_M((I23+J23) tensor(I25+J25)).
+These matrices are invertible over Q, since det(I_h+J_h)=h+1. This is one
+explicit rational basis for every physical role and operation. All required
+controlled permutations and both full restriction trees are checked by the
+inherited pinned geometry code; none is reselected for an individual pair.
+
+For a source triple indicator t in dimension h, the retained H=I-J/9 form
+has norm2 on t. Its conjugated line projector is v nu where
+ v=t+3*1,
+ nu=(t-10/[3(h+1)]*1)^t/2.
+Every primal and dual coordinate is nonzero at h23 and25. Their products are
+ h23:31/18 on the triple, -5/24 outside;
+ h25:68/39 on the triple, -5/26 outside.
+The sums are respectively3*(31/18)+20*(-5/24)=1 and
+3*(68/39)+22*(-5/26)=1. The Python verifier checks all1,771+2,300 individual
+triple lines exactly, without inference from random sampling.
+
+2. Actual local and auxiliary transfers
+
+The pinned controlled permutations give the following entry identities.
+On first23/last23 coordinates, A tensor(v nu) has corner
+ diag(v_i) A diag(nu_(j+2)), i,j=0,...,22.
+On first25/last25 coordinates, (p xi) tensor B has corner
+ diag(p_(r_i)) B diag(xi_(c_j)),
+ r=(0,...,22,22,0), c=(22,0,0,...,22).
+These formulas hold for ANY matrices A and B. The verifier checks the actual
+permutation indices, not just a symbolic tensor rank. Since all actual source
+line evaluations in Section1 are nonzero, every actual fixed first/second
+local ordered profile transfers through nonzero diagonal scalings. Setting
+A or B to the identity gives the unchanged diagonal auxiliary corners. The
+rank-one fronts and corank-one growth fronts keep their retained profiles;
+the latter use the nonzero extreme pivot and central identity block after
+cancelling the rank-one term. Generic ordinary profiles must NOT be used to
+replace either axis's separately certified fixed internal profile.
+
+3. Actual data matrix and universal zero identities
+
+For each actual pair(T,S) of source triples, write P=p xi,Q=v nu. The null
+corner of(I-P) tensor(I-Q) is, after nonzero row and column scalings,
+ M_ij=[R_i=C_j]/z_(R_i)+[beta_i=gamma_j]/w_(beta_i)-1,
+ z_r=p_r xi_r,w_t=v_t nu_t,
+ beta_i=i mod25,gamma_j=(528+j)mod25=(j+3)mod25.
+The data projector itself has the negative of this off-diagonal corner,
+which preserves its ordered profile. Both boundary restriction graphs are
+trees, giving full nullity47 and the large-projector identity middle481.
+
+The ordered pivot list is
+ (0,46);
+ (i,i+24), i=1,...,21;
+ (22,24),(23,23),(24,22),(25,21),(26,20),(27,19);
+ (i,i-26), i=28,...,44;
+ (45,1),(46,0).
+The inherited PR34 rank-cut identities, independently checked over integers
+at h23 in PR37, hold for EVERY choice of the diagonal weights. They prove
+all right-of-pivot zeros needed by this list. These identities survive both
+fixed specializations. The extra modular zero checks below are regressions;
+the zero proof is not inferred from residues. Descending singleton steps
+have no unselected column to their right.
+
+4. Exhaustive nonvanishing, with valid bad-prime fallback
+
+geometry.cpp enumerates the Cartesian product of all1,771 first triples and
+all2,300 second triples, without filtering or symmetry reduction. For each
+pair it constructs the actual scaled matrix above and attempts the ENTIRE
+47-pivot elimination modulo1000003. If a prescribed pivot vanishes, it
+reinitializes the matrix and repeats the ENTIRE sequence at2147483647, then
+at1000000007 if necessary. A pair is counted only after one complete replay
+has47 nonzero pivots. An unresolved pair fails the run, never disappearing
+from the certificate. Every chosen prime is checked by trial division;
+scaled weight/reciprocal denominators are invertible at all of them. All
+products fit signed64-bit arithmetic; matrix initialization also uses64-bit
+storage before reduction, preventing31-bit-prime addition overflow.
+
+Why this proves the rational claim: at an admissible prime, a nonzero residue
+of a rational prefix minor implies that minor is nonzero over Q. A complete
+successful replay therefore proves all47 actual rational prefix minors for
+that pair. Different pairs may use different witness primes. No common
+witness prime, CRT magnitude bound, or numerical positivity assumption is
+needed for this one-sided implication. The eventual machine address prime
+is chosen separately, after all rational matrices are fixed, avoiding the
+finitely many bad denominators and nonzero minors.
+
+The complete result is:
+ actual pairs                    4073300
+ nonzero ordered prefixes      191445100
+ ordered-zero regression checks1409361800
+ successful pairs at1000003      4073290
+ successful pairs at2147483647        10
+ successful pairs at1000000007         0
+ unresolved pairs                       0
+Every primary-prime zero event is preserved with pair index, both triples,
+failed step and successful fallback prime. The Python verifier additionally
+replays ALL10 such pairs over Q, proving that each primary zero was accidental.
+For example T={0,9,10},S={14,18,20}, step(26,20), has exact nonzero pivot
+ -1040817578056012397961768075264/140132077459481987775304655993.
+Its numerator vanishes modulo1000003; its complete rational21+17 profile
+still survives. Treating that residue as a rational zero would be incorrect.
+
+The initial complete run took85.894 seconds. The archived timing/source/output
+hash receipt is kept as provenance in geometry-source.json; timing is not a
+proof field or an expected time for another machine. The C++ file is retained
+byte-for-byte from that completed run. geometry.py --full provides a portable
+fresh replay and exact comparison of the deterministic mathematical output.
+The default verifies its pins, complete coverage, exact local/complement
+controls and all10 rational fallback controls; it does not claim a fresh
+multi-million-pair replay. No millions of individual raw records are needed:
+the exhaustive loop, final count assertions, compact fallback list and
+portable complete replay establish coverage.
+
+5. Both sets of copied-center complements
+
+For each retained U_i=ker(1^t-3e_i^t) in h23 or25, its H-orthogonal complement
+has normalized projector p_i xi_i with
+ p_i=e_i+2/(h-9)*1,
+ xi_i=(h-9)/12*(1^t-3e_i^t).
+Indeed H p_i=e_i-(1/3)*1 and xi_i p_i=1. After fixing L_h=I+J, the pair is
+ p'_i=e_i+(3h-7)/(h-9)*1,
+ xi'_i=(h-9)/[3(h+1)]*1^t-(h-9)/4*e_i^t.
+Thus at h23 the pair is ei+31/7*1 and7/36*1^t-7/2*ei^t; at h25 it is
+ei+17/4*1 and8/39*1^t-4*ei^t. Every coordinate is nonzero and the pairing
+is one. The Python verifier checks all48 complements exactly. Section2's
+arbitrary-matrix transfer includes every such fixed rank-one projector.
+
+For each dimension h, retain the ENTIRE original-envelope fixed-basis
+internal transition profile, including the actual ordered profile of each
+rank-(h-1) copied transform. The copied-center update removes exactly h old
+identity width-h cleanup calls and adds h rank-one complement calls. It does
+not delete the copied residual, apply a generic-rank expansion to its fixed
+matrix, or add the new profile on top of the old one. Both local profiles
+must be freshly certified from their actual producer/matching multiset.
+
+6. Physical and theorem boundary
+
+The21-block is physically rows1..21/columns553..573; the17-block is
+rows28..44/columns530..546. Both are disjoint from the481 middle at47..527.
+No runtime gather or free basis reordering is inserted. The inherited
+lower-triangular compiler therefore realizes these exact contiguous blocks.
+This explicit common basis needs no generic factor or finite-product claim.
+All remaining local matrices are handled by their complete fixed-profile
+certificates and the exact transfer identities, not by a generic assumption.
+
+Copied-stream restoration, retained scalar circuits, source/sink operators,
+row/spectator volumes, endpoint copies and all inherited analytic/fixed-tape
+interfaces remain separate obligations. Their costs must appear in the full
+new characteristic and assembly. This finite geometry certificate alone does
+not prove an unconditional multiplication bound or global optimality.
